 Replay to reach the others.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ascension</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Martyrdom</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Corrupted Immortality</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And more<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4068230/extras/3c7e349d6faf83e63c13afc588a1a819.avif?t=1786389761\" width=1170 height=70 /></span></p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Lovecraftian psychological detective horror</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The world is the interface. No HUD, no menus</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Minimal text and voice. Symbols and the world itself do the talking</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Context-aware controls with zero menu transitions</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Lo-fi visuals, heavy atmosphere, runs on weak PCs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Survival through knowledge and rituals, not combat</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Endings shaped by your choices and what your sanity survives</p></li></ul>", "short_description": "You are the Void Priest, bound to an Elder God against your will. Guided only by relics, symbols, and light, solve eldritch mysteries and perform forbidden rituals. Survive long enough to choose whether you stay faithful or betray.", "supported_languages": "English, French, Italian, German, Spanish - Spain, Arabic, Bulgarian, Czech, Danish, Dutch, Finnish, Greek, Hungarian, Indonesian, Japanese, Korean, Norwegian, Polish, Portuguese - Brazil, Portuguese - Portugal, Romanian, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish - Latin America, Swedish, Thai, Traditional Chinese, Turkish, Ukrainian, Vietnamese, Afrikaans, Albanian, Amharic, Armenian, Assamese, Azerbaijani, Bangla, Basque, Belarusian, Bosnian, Catalan, Cherokee, Croatian, Dari, Estonian, Filipino, Galician, Georgian, Gujarati, Ha